# TypeScript-only source

All extension logic under `src/` and all repo scripts under `scripts/` must be **TypeScript** (`.ts`). Do not add JavaScript source files (`.js`, `.jsx`, `.mjs`) under those directories.

- **Allowed:** root TypeScript tooling (`esbuild.config.ts`, `eslint.config.ts`, `vitest.config.ts`), compiled output in `out/`, generated assets, and other non-source files.
- **Run via:** [tsx](https://github.com/privatenumber/tsx) — no pre-compile step for tooling.
- **Enforced by:** `tsconfig.json` / `tsconfig.tools.json` (`allowJs: false`), ESLint overrides for forbidden extensions, `npm run check:typescript-only`, and CI.

When adding new code, use `.ts` and match existing module/style conventions in the repo.
